#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:108
#: 37f9b7cefe514ca3b725336c2e3ba35b
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:110
#: a14abc66229b4b4ea3c9885b5bcf3c40
msgid "The mouse sensor returns the average movement (in the x and y directions) of surface features that it sees. A single pixel move will not cause the sensor to return \"1\". It will return a higher value around 5. This value is referred to as the **scaler** below. In the example below, the value returned would be about 1.6 ( (-5+5+5) / 3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:119
#: 1fa3e54f6e754d0a99f680f3ab6b073e
msgid "**Sensor's x and y values can be converted to real distances based on altitude**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:122
#: 9afe399ad3b24b729a78723f2643be53
msgid "In order to convert values from the sensor to real distances moved, we need to take into account the altitude. This is necessary because as you can see from the two pictures below, if we have two quads moving the same distance, but one at a low altitude, the other at a higher altitude, the lower quad will see surface features appear to move further and this will result in a higher optical flow values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:135
#: d1c3630a71cf4d388736b89814e2a836
msgid "We compensate for vehicle roll and pitch changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:137
#: 6f3a60fe64394d66af6f95294f87de40
msgid "Change in the vehicle's roll and pitch will also cause changes in the x and y values returned by the sensor. Unlike the lateral movement calculations these are not dependent upon the distance of the visible objects. In the picture below you can see that as the quad has rolled 10 degrees but both flowers have moved from the center of the camera's view in the 1st pic to the edge of the view in the 2nd pic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:147
#: c957fe4fa3494fa48a70ff9829633990
msgid "The expected change in sensor values can be calculated directly from the change in roll and pitch given the formula below. We subtract these expected changes from the real values returned by the sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mouse-based-optical-flow-sensor-adns3080.rst:154
#: 7b7634eb8a5f453b871cb090c6350a62
msgid "Once we have the x/y movements we can integrate these values over time with the current yaw to arrive at an estimate of position."
msgstr ""

